## 4. Exclusion List

These items must not appear in the draft.

- AI versus human workforce replacement narrative. John explicitly pushed back on this framing and it dilutes the "amplify your DNA" thesis.
- Generic AI statistics and market size projections not tied to John's direct experience or sourced Improving client work.
- Vendor comparisons or platform recommendations. John intentionally avoided naming winners.
- Technical explanations of how LLMs work internally. The target audience (CTO/VP level) does not need this.
- "AI is transformational" framing that implies companies must reinvent themselves. This is the villain, not the recommendation.
- 101-level prompting tutorials. The transcript touched on prompting but as a secondary aside, not a thesis point.
- Industry-by-industry breakdown as the primary organizing frame. John's thesis is universal regardless of industry; organizing by vertical would bury the lead.
- The "if you're not paying, you are the product" line as a standalone section. It's a good pull quote but not a section anchor.

