Section note: The strongest demonstrated ROI from AI right now is in surfacing knowledge from large, previously unsearchable content libraries. This is not glamorous. It is also not automation. It is the retrieval and synthesis work that humans either skip or do badly because it is tedious. Education company story here. HVAC/roofing example as contrast: completely different industry, same principle.

- H3: The content that existed but was functionally invisible
  Section note: The education company setup and solution. The "sixth ring of hell" line (the host's, attributed informally) earns its place here: humans get bored, AI does not, and that asymmetry is the actual business case.
